   $q$For what value of $a$ does the system $y = ax + 3$ and $4x - 2y = 7$ have no solution?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$a = -\\frac{1}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-negative-reciprocal"},{"text":"$a = -2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-solving-for-y"},{"text":"$a = 2$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$a = 4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-x-coefficient-as-slope"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$a = 2$$q$, $q$Solve the second equation for $y$: $-2y = -4x + 7$, so $y = 2x - \frac{7}{2}$. Its slope is $2$. Lines with equal slopes and different $y$-intercepts ($3$ and $-\frac{7}{2}$) are parallel, so $a = 2$. The value $-\frac{1}{2}$ is the slope of a perpendicular line, which would cross at one point.$q$, 'draft', null)
