   $q$A barn holds only chickens and goats. Altogether the animals have 30 heads and 84 legs. How many goats are in the barn?$q$, $q$[{"text":"12","is_correct":true},{"text":"21","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-legs-by-four"},{"text":"15","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-equal-split"},{"text":"18","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-the-other-unknown"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$12$q$, $q$Let $c$ be chickens and $g$ be goats: $c + g = 30$ and $2c + 4g = 84$. Multiply the first equation by $2$: $2c + 2g = 60$. Subtract it from the second: $2g = 24$, so $g = 12$. The value 18 is the number of chickens.$q$, 'draft', null)
