   $q$Ana buys 3 bagels and 2 muffins for 11 dollars. Ben buys 1 bagel and 4 muffins for 12 dollars. If $b$ is the cost of one bagel and $m$ is the cost of one muffin, in dollars, which system models the situation?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$b + m = 11$ and $b + m = 12$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-quantities"},{"text":"$3b + 2m = 12$ and $b + 4m = 11$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-totals"},{"text":"$2b + 3m = 11$ and $4b + m = 12$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"paired-counts-with-wrong-items"},{"text":"$3b + 2m = 11$ and $b + 4m = 12$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$3b + 2m = 11$ and $b + 4m = 12$$q$, $q$Ana's purchase costs $3b + 2m$, which equals 11 dollars, and Ben's costs $1b + 4m$, which equals 12 dollars. So the system is $3b + 2m = 11$ and $b + 4m = 12$. The system with $2b + 3m$ attaches the number of muffins to the bagel price.$q$, 'draft', null)
