   $q$A $16$-foot ladder leans against a vertical wall and makes a $70^\circ$ angle with the level ground. How high up the wall does the top of the ladder reach, to the nearest tenth of a foot?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$5.5$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-cosine-for-opposite-side"},{"text":"$15.0$ feet","is_correct":true},{"text":"$44.0$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-tangent-with-hypotenuse"},{"text":"$17.0$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-by-sine"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$15.0$ feet$q$, $q$The ladder is the hypotenuse, and the height on the wall is opposite the $70^\circ$ angle at the ground, so $h = 16\sin 70^\circ \approx 15.0$ feet. The value $5.5$ feet is $16\cos 70^\circ$, which is the distance from the wall to the foot of the ladder.$q$, 'draft', null)
