   $q$A kite string is pulled straight and is $50$ meters long from the hand to the kite. The string makes a $40^\circ$ angle with the horizontal. Ignoring the height of the hand, which equation gives the height $h$ of the kite in meters?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$h = 50\\tan 40^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-tangent-with-hypotenuse"},{"text":"$h = 50\\cos 40^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-cosine-for-opposite-side"},{"text":"$h = \\frac{50}{\\sin 40^\\circ}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-by-sine"},{"text":"$h = 50\\sin 40^\\circ$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$h = 50\sin 40^\circ$$q$, $q$The string is the hypotenuse and the height is the side opposite the $40^\circ$ angle, so $\sin 40^\circ = \frac{h}{50}$ and $h = 50\sin 40^\circ$. The equation $h = 50\cos 40^\circ$ gives the horizontal distance, the side adjacent to the angle.$q$, 'draft', null)
