  ('1f673c7f-5a85-5e40-8d03-30899548f81f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'similarity-right-triangles'), null, 'medium',
   $q$From the top of a cliff $45$ meters above the water, Tomasz sights a boat. The angle of depression from the top of the cliff to the boat is $18^\circ$. What is the horizontal distance from the base of the cliff to the boat, to the nearest tenth of a meter?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$138.5$ meters","is_correct":true},{"text":"$42.8$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-cosine-instead-of-tangent"},{"text":"$14.6$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-depression-angle-at-cliff-top-vertex"},{"text":"$145.6$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-line-of-sight-not-horizontal-distance"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$138.5$ meters$q$, $q$The angle of depression equals the angle of elevation from the boat up to the cliff top, $18^\circ$. At the boat, the cliff height $45$ is opposite and the horizontal distance $d$ is adjacent, so $\tan 18^\circ = \frac{45}{d}$ and $d = \frac{45}{\tan 18^\circ} \approx 138.5$ meters. The value $14.6$ meters treats $18^\circ$ as the angle at the cliff top, between the cliff and the line of sight.$q$, 'draft', null)
