   $q$A straight ramp is $14$ feet long, measured along its sloped surface, and its top end is $3$ feet above the level ground. What angle does the ramp make with the ground, to the nearest tenth of a degree?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$0.2^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reported-ratio-instead-of-angle"},{"text":"$77.6^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-cosine-gave-complement"},{"text":"$12.1^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-tangent-with-hypotenuse"},{"text":"$12.4^\\circ$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$12.4^\circ$$q$, $q$The $3$-foot rise is opposite the angle and the $14$-foot ramp is the hypotenuse, so $\sin\theta = \frac{3}{14}$ and $\theta = \sin^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{14}\right) \approx 12.4^\circ$. The value $12.1^\circ$ uses inverse tangent, but $14$ is the hypotenuse, not the horizontal run.$q$, 'draft', null)
