   $q$A $20$-foot ladder must reach a window ledge $18$ feet above level ground on a vertical wall. How far from the base of the wall should the foot of the ladder be placed, to the nearest tenth of a foot?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$76$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-square-root"},{"text":"$26.9$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-squares-when-finding-a-leg"},{"text":"$2$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-lengths-not-squares"},{"text":"$8.7$ feet","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$8.7$ feet$q$, $q$The ladder is the hypotenuse, so $d = \sqrt{20^2 - 18^2} = \sqrt{400 - 324} = \sqrt{76} \approx 8.7$ feet. The value $26.9$ feet adds the squares, but a leg is found by subtracting from the square of the hypotenuse.$q$, 'draft', null)
