  ('3e5368a1-1f95-5499-a0e6-65d2d93308f3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'similarity-right-triangles'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Right triangle $PQR$ has its right angle at $R$. The altitude from $R$ meets hypotenuse $PQ$ at point $S$, splitting it into $PS = 4$ and $SQ = 9$. The two smaller triangles are similar to each other and to $PQR$. What is the length of $RS$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$13$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-the-segments"},{"text":"$36$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-square-root"},{"text":"$6.5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"averaged-the-segments"},{"text":"$6$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$6$$q$, $q$From the similar triangles $PSR$ and $RSQ$, $\frac{PS}{RS} = \frac{RS}{SQ}$, so $RS^2 = 4 \cdot 9 = 36$ and $RS = 6$. The value $6.5$ is the ordinary average of $4$ and $9$, but similarity gives the geometric mean.$q$, 'draft', null)
