  ('fb36f29d-20fc-5687-ac39-db023e81bec5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'similarity-right-triangles'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Amara's eyes are $1.5$ meters above level ground. Standing $25$ meters from the base of a tree, Amara measures the angle of elevation from eye level to the top of the tree as $32^\circ$. How tall is the tree, to the nearest tenth of a meter?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$41.5$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-by-tangent"},{"text":"$14.7$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-sine-instead-of-tangent"},{"text":"$17.1$ meters","is_correct":true},{"text":"$15.6$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-add-eye-height"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$17.1$ meters$q$, $q$Above eye level, the tree rises $25\tan 32^\circ \approx 15.62$ meters, since that part is opposite the angle and the $25$ meters is adjacent. Add the eye height: $15.62 + 1.5 \approx 17.1$ meters. The value $15.6$ meters measures only from eye level, not from the ground.$q$, 'draft', null)
