  ('1fbb6520-bbfc-5c29-bb13-9f9ca68c24e9', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'similarity-right-triangles'), null, 'medium',
   $q$A ladder leans against a vertical wall and makes a $60^\circ$ angle with the level ground. The foot of the ladder is $5$ feet from the wall. What is the exact length of the ladder?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{5}{2}$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-by-cosine-instead-of-dividing"},{"text":"$5\\sqrt{3}$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-height-on-wall-instead"},{"text":"$10$ feet","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-sine-for-adjacent-side"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$10$ feet$q$, $q$The $5$ feet along the ground is adjacent to the $60^\circ$ angle and the ladder is the hypotenuse, so $L = \frac{5}{\cos 60^\circ} = \frac{5}{\frac{1}{2}} = 10$ feet. This is a 30, 60, 90 triangle whose shorter leg is $5$. The value $5\sqrt{3}$ feet is the height the ladder reaches on the wall.$q$, 'draft', null)
