  ('550a9a2d-5f50-5232-adf2-7c24074a7d2f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'similarity-right-triangles'), null, 'medium',
   $q$A closed box is $12$ inches long, $9$ inches wide and $8$ inches tall. What is the length of the longest straight rod that fits inside, running from one bottom corner to the opposite top corner?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$17$ inches","is_correct":true},{"text":"$29$ inches","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-the-dimensions"},{"text":"$289$ inches","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-square-root"},{"text":"$15$ inches","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-only-the-base-diagonal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$17$ inches$q$, $q$First the bottom diagonal: $\sqrt{12^2 + 9^2} = 15$. That diagonal and the height $8$ are the legs of a second right triangle, so the rod is $\sqrt{15^2 + 8^2} = \sqrt{289} = 17$ inches. The value $15$ inches stops at the floor of the box.$q$, 'draft', null)
