  ('66c06abb-6313-5924-bea1-e48172e65926', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'similarity-right-triangles'), null, 'hard',
   $q$From point $A$ on level ground, the angle of elevation to the top of a tower is $30^\circ$. Walking $40$ meters straight toward the tower to point $B$, the angle of elevation becomes $45^\circ$. How tall is the tower, to the nearest tenth of a meter?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$54.6$ meters","is_correct":true},{"text":"$23.1$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-only-the-walk-distance"},{"text":"$94.6$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-distance-from-point-a-not-height"},{"text":"$40$ meters","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-height-equals-walk-distance"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$54.6$ meters$q$, $q$Let $h$ be the height. At $B$, $\tan 45^\circ = 1$, so $B$ is $h$ meters from the base, and $A$ is $h + 40$ meters away. At $A$, $\tan 30^\circ = \frac{h}{h + 40}$, so $h\sqrt{3} = h + 40$ and $h = \frac{40}{\sqrt{3} - 1} \approx 54.6$ meters. The value $94.6$ meters is $h + 40$, the distance from $A$ to the base.$q$, 'draft', null)
