   $q$Subtract: $(6x^2 + 2x - 4) - (3x^2 - 5x + 1)$. Which polynomial is the difference?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$3x^2 + 7x - 5$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$9x^2 - 3x - 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-instead-of-subtracted"},{"text":"$3x^2 + 7x - 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-negate-constant"},{"text":"$3x^2 - 3x - 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-first-term-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$3x^2 + 7x - 5$$q$, $q$Subtracting a polynomial means subtracting every term, so the second polynomial becomes $-3x^2 + 5x - 1$. Then $6x^2 - 3x^2 = 3x^2$, $2x + 5x = 7x$, and $-4 - 1 = -5$, giving $3x^2 + 7x - 5$. The choice $3x^2 - 3x - 3$ changes the sign of only the first term.$q$, 'draft', null)
