   $q$In an arithmetic sequence with first term $a_1$, $a_3 = 11$ and $a_8 = 31$. Which explicit formula, for $n \geq 1$, describes the sequence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$a_n = 4n + 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-first-term-as-constant-without-shifting"},{"text":"$a_n = 11 + 4(n-1)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-a-later-term-as-first-term"},{"text":"$a_n = 5n - 4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-index-gap-as-difference"},{"text":"$a_n = 4n - 1$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$a_n = 4n - 1$$q$, $q$From $a_3$ to $a_8$ is $5$ steps and the value rises by $31 - 11 = 20$, so $d = \frac{20}{5} = 4$. Then $a_1 = 11 - 2(4) = 3$, and $a_n = 3 + 4(n-1) = 4n - 1$. Check: $4(8) - 1 = 31$. The formula $4n + 3$ gives $7$ at $n = 1$, because the $3$ is the first term and must go with $n - 1$, not $n$.$q$, 'draft', null)
