   $q$With $x$ in radians, what is the period of $y = 2\cos(3x)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$6\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-2pi-by-b"},{"text":"$\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"divided-by-the-amplitude"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{2\\pi}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-the-period-formula"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{2\pi}{3}$$q$, $q$For $y = a\cos(bx)$ the period is $\frac{2\pi}{|b|}$. Here $b = 3$, so the period is $\frac{2\pi}{3}$. The choice $6\pi$ multiplies by $3$, but a larger $b$ squeezes the graph, so the period gets shorter.$q$, 'draft', null)
