   $q$Which angle between $0$ and $2\pi$ radians is coterminal with $-\frac{5\pi}{4}$ radians?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{13\\pi}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"computed-2pi-minus-the-angle"},{"text":"$\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-the-reference-angle"},{"text":"$\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-the-negative-sign"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{3\pi}{4}$$q$, $q$Coterminal angles differ by full turns of $2\pi$. Add $2\pi = \frac{8\pi}{4}$: $-\frac{5\pi}{4} + \frac{8\pi}{4} = \frac{3\pi}{4}$, which is between $0$ and $2\pi$. The choice $\frac{5\pi}{4}$ just drops the sign, but turning $\frac{5\pi}{4}$ clockwise ends in Quadrant II, not Quadrant III.$q$, 'draft', null)
