   $q$The angle $-\frac{11\pi}{3}$ is in radians. What is $\sin\left(-\frac{11\pi}{3}\right)$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-sine-and-cosine"},{"text":"$\\sqrt{3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"computed-tangent-instead"},{"text":"$-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-negative-angle"},{"text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$$q$, $q$Add two full turns, $4\pi = \frac{12\pi}{3}$: $-\frac{11\pi}{3} + \frac{12\pi}{3} = \frac{\pi}{3}$. So $\sin\left(-\frac{11\pi}{3}\right) = \sin\frac{\pi}{3} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$. The choice $-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$ is $\sin\frac{11\pi}{3}$, the value for the positive angle.$q$, 'draft', null)
